1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,420
Here's the request every BA has seen.

2
00:00:03,740 --> 00:00:07,500
We need an AI agent for invoice approvals.

3
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:09,780
Then you look at the process.

4
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:12,460
It's three rules and a spreadsheet.

5
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:14,280
That's not an agent.

6
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:17,440
That's an IF statement wearing a blazer.

7
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:20,400
And it's an expensive mix-up,

8
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:25,540
Gartner expects over 40% of agentic AI projects to

9
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:28,060
be cancelled by the end of 2027.

10
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:32,340
And it says many use cases pitched as agentic

11
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:34,420
don't need an agent at all.

12
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:39,780
Gartner even has a name for relabeling chatbots and

13
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:41,880
old automations as agents.

14
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:43,760
Agent washing.

15
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:49,440
It estimates only about 130 of the thousands of

16
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:51,900
agentic AI vendors are a real thing.

17
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:54,180
I'm Prachit,

18
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:55,400
a Business Analyst.

19
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:57,880
Today, three levels of automation,

20
00:00:58,220 --> 00:00:59,340
five questions,

21
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:02,940
and one test that quietly kills half of the

22
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:04,640
agent ideas in the meeting.

23
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:06,980
It's question four.

24
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:09,280
First, the levels.

25
00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:11,580
Level 1 is rules.

26
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:12,980
Same input,

27
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:14,240
same output,

28
00:01:14,460 --> 00:01:15,360
a workflow,

29
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:16,360
a formula,

30
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:19,060
a bot that clicks the same buttons.

31
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:23,400
Level 2 is AI that reads messy inputs and

32
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:24,260
makes a judgment.

33
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:26,140
Label this email.

34
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:28,520
Pull the total off this PDF.

35
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:31,160
Level 3 is an agent.

36
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:36,000
AI that takes actions across systems several steps on

37
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:36,400
its own.

38
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:38,460
Think vending machine,

39
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:39,540
translator,

40
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:42,360
and a new hire with a company card.

41
00:01:42,767 --> 00:01:44,287
Question 1.

42
00:01:44,547 --> 00:01:47,627
Can you write the decision as rules on one

43
00:01:47,327 --> 00:01:47,947
page?

44
00:01:48,707 --> 00:01:49,587
If yes,

45
00:01:49,827 --> 00:01:50,547
stop.

46
00:01:51,167 --> 00:01:52,307
Build the rules.

47
00:01:52,807 --> 00:01:53,607
They're cheaper,

48
00:01:53,887 --> 00:01:55,207
they're easier to test,

49
00:01:55,347 --> 00:01:57,207
and they never hallucinate.

50
00:01:57,727 --> 00:02:02,607
Quote, I approve invoices under $500 that match a

51
00:02:02,307 --> 00:02:03,227
purchase order.

52
00:02:03,607 --> 00:02:05,527
It doesn't need a personality.

53
00:02:05,847 --> 00:02:08,527
And if nobody can write the rules because they

54
00:02:08,227 --> 00:02:09,507
change every Tuesday,

55
00:02:10,027 --> 00:02:11,407
that's a different problem.

56
00:02:11,887 --> 00:02:13,967
The policy isn't decided yet,

57
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:17,147
no model fixes an undecided policy.

58
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:19,080
Question 2.

59
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:21,140
Is the input messy?

60
00:02:21,980 --> 00:02:23,540
Free text emails,

61
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,620
scanned PDFs,

62
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:26,540
voicemails,

63
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:29,220
that's where AI earns its keep.

64
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:31,720
But if the input is clean form,

65
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:35,440
the best AI project might be fixing the form.

66
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:41,020
Turn the free text box into a dropdown and

67
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:43,120
half the AI problem disappears.

68
00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:46,660
Sometimes the right AI is a dropdown.

69
00:02:46,967 --> 00:02:51,307
Question three does it need to act or just

70
00:02:51,007 --> 00:02:51,787
recommend.

71
00:02:52,927 --> 00:02:55,567
Reading and suggesting is level two.

72
00:02:55,827 --> 00:02:59,307
Clicking approve in three systems is level three.

73
00:02:59,867 --> 00:03:03,067
Every action you add is one more thing that

74
00:03:02,767 --> 00:03:05,167
can go wrong in production at 2 a.m.

75
00:03:05,227 --> 00:03:07,707
with nobody watching but the logs.

76
00:03:08,133 --> 00:03:09,553
Question 4.

77
00:03:09,873 --> 00:03:10,913
The one I promised.

78
00:03:11,333 --> 00:03:12,533
The undo test.

79
00:03:13,013 --> 00:03:14,233
If it gets it wrong,

80
00:03:14,373 --> 00:03:15,553
can you undo it?

81
00:03:16,033 --> 00:03:17,893
A draft that a person reviews.

82
00:03:18,773 --> 00:03:19,913
It's an easy undo.

83
00:03:20,373 --> 00:03:21,233
A refund.

84
00:03:21,473 --> 00:03:22,573
A deleted record.

85
00:03:22,933 --> 00:03:25,273
An email to 10,000 customers.

86
00:03:25,813 --> 00:03:27,093
No undo.

87
00:03:27,153 --> 00:03:29,933
There's no Ctrl+Z for an email blast.

88
00:03:30,233 --> 00:03:35,953
Ask anyone who sent the test version of the

89
00:03:35,653 --> 00:03:36,493
whole list.

90
00:03:36,193 --> 00:03:40,173
No undo means a person approves the action every

91
00:03:39,873 --> 00:03:40,493
time.

92
00:03:40,833 --> 00:03:42,193
Question 5.

93
00:03:42,513 --> 00:03:43,913
Can you measure better?

94
00:03:44,533 --> 00:03:46,193
Time per case,

95
00:03:46,273 --> 00:03:47,153
error rate,

96
00:03:47,113 --> 00:03:48,353
cost per case,

97
00:03:48,413 --> 00:03:51,313
measure them today before anything gets built.

98
00:03:51,393 --> 00:03:52,333
No baseline,

99
00:03:52,733 --> 00:03:53,973
no business case.

100
00:03:54,553 --> 00:03:57,373
Otherwise, in six months somebody asks,

101
00:03:57,373 --> 00:03:58,573
did the AI work?

102
00:03:58,853 --> 00:04:01,353
And the honest answer is a vibe.

103
00:04:01,733 --> 00:04:05,513
Let's run it on our made-up client Northstar Systems.

104
00:04:05,993 --> 00:04:07,293
Invoice matching.

105
00:04:07,513 --> 00:04:09,133
The rules fit on one page.

106
00:04:09,693 --> 00:04:10,753
Level 1.

107
00:04:11,053 --> 00:04:14,313
No agent and the vendor demo goes back in

108
00:04:14,013 --> 00:04:14,733
the drawer.

109
00:04:14,973 --> 00:04:15,853
Refund emails.

110
00:04:16,353 --> 00:04:17,413
Messy input,

111
00:04:17,593 --> 00:04:19,393
but it only needs to recommend.

112
00:04:20,393 --> 00:04:21,693
Level 2.

113
00:04:22,133 --> 00:04:26,353
And a person approves chasing vendors for missing invoices.

114
00:04:26,053 --> 00:04:30,633
messy replies and it sends emails and updates a

115
00:04:30,333 --> 00:04:31,013
tracker.

116
00:04:31,493 --> 00:04:35,373
Level 3 with the person approving the first message

117
00:04:35,073 --> 00:04:36,233
to each vendor.

118
00:04:36,667 --> 00:04:38,187
Three processes,

119
00:04:38,467 --> 00:04:41,467
three different answers from the same five questions.

120
00:04:41,827 --> 00:04:42,907
That's the point.

121
00:04:43,207 --> 00:04:44,667
Should we use AI?

122
00:04:45,627 --> 00:04:47,147
Is the wrong question.

123
00:04:47,487 --> 00:04:49,927
Which level does this process need?

124
00:04:50,067 --> 00:04:51,147
Is the right one?

125
00:04:51,433 --> 00:04:55,353
I put five questions on a one-page scoring sheet

126
00:04:55,053 --> 00:04:56,713
in my BA Toolkit,

127
00:04:56,893 --> 00:04:58,773
free linked in the description.

128
00:04:59,153 --> 00:05:02,053
Bring it to the next meeting where someone says,

129
00:05:02,093 --> 00:05:04,393
Agent, in the first five minutes.

130
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:06,260
Bonus trick,

131
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:07,800
and it's a fun one,

132
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:11,580
paste the process into an AI model and ask

133
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:13,680
it to argue against using an agent,

134
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,140
not for it,

135
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:16,100
against.

136
00:05:17,620 --> 00:05:20,420
Models are great at building whatever case you ask

137
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:20,700
for,

138
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:23,460
so ask for one you need to hear.

139
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:25,940
If it's best arguments holds up,

140
00:05:26,180 --> 00:05:27,820
you just saved a budget line.

141
00:05:28,133 --> 00:05:31,013
And don't walk into that meeting with a flat

142
00:05:30,713 --> 00:05:31,453
no.

143
00:05:31,673 --> 00:05:34,753
Say, let's start one level down and earn the

144
00:05:34,453 --> 00:05:35,293
next one.

145
00:05:35,533 --> 00:05:36,553
Rules first,

146
00:05:36,833 --> 00:05:37,773
then AI,

147
00:05:37,913 --> 00:05:40,793
then an agent that acts.

148
00:05:41,353 --> 00:05:44,433
Once the numbers from level 2 say it's ready,

149
00:05:44,693 --> 00:05:47,313
nobody argues with a plan that ends in a

150
00:05:47,013 --> 00:05:47,613
yes.

151
00:05:48,033 --> 00:05:50,833
The level also changes what you write.

152
00:05:51,033 --> 00:05:51,953
At level 2,

153
00:05:51,733 --> 00:05:54,173
acceptance criteria becomes pass rates.

154
00:05:54,213 --> 00:05:55,373
At level 3,

155
00:05:55,253 --> 00:05:57,313
you also need the never rules,

156
00:05:57,473 --> 00:05:59,853
what the agent must never do on its own.

157
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:02,880
So, can you write the rules?

158
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,740
Is the input messy?

159
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:06,380
Does it need to act?

160
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:08,040
Can you undo it?

161
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:09,820
And can you measure better?

162
00:06:10,260 --> 00:06:11,540
Five questions,

163
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:12,660
three levels.

164
00:06:13,167 --> 00:06:14,487
Quiz time!

165
00:06:14,907 --> 00:06:17,347
Six questions popping up right now,

166
00:06:17,447 --> 00:06:18,567
easy to hard,

167
00:06:18,827 --> 00:06:20,027
how many can you get?

168
00:06:54,433 --> 00:06:59,233
Then tell me what's the most over-engineered AI request

169
00:06:58,933 --> 00:07:02,233
you've seen at work and if your product already

170
00:07:01,933 --> 00:07:06,353
has an agent The never rules video is next
